# Everything here is generated. `make_tickets.py` is seeded, so the corpus
# reproduces byte-identically and there is nothing to gain from committing it.
#
# This also matters for safety rather than tidiness: with *.jsonl ignored, a real
# customer export dropped into this folder to try a run cannot be committed by
# accident. Putting it in git would need a deliberate `git add -f`.
*.jsonl
